{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3107","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3107","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3107\",\"parent_revision\":\"49b7b1a83b6f64e8542209a19477b4176d204234\",\"root_revision\":\"a3c28ba29721dd660c5ef6bad899638287cf2edad287e6ccb6030f8e64a7a3bd\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: Ideas\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-21\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThis is an exploration/experiment item \u2014 its deliverable is an experiment result or design decision with evidence (a prototype on a real plan, a measured comparison, or a written design verdict), not a mandate to ship a feature.\\n\\nOrigin: mechanism mined from Claude Code's built-in ultracode Workflow orchestration system \u2014 a code-executed multi-agent workflow runtime whose design contract contains several simple-but-effective patterns DH can adopt without adopting the runtime itself.\\n\\nShared design constraint (same as #3097\u2013#3103): the model keeps the judgment but writes it down once, as typed data, at planning time; the mechanical consequence is applied deterministically by machinery that already exists. No new scheduler, no generic graph runtime \u2014 out of scope.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **explore refute-framed verification votes in quality gates** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: ultracode Workflow orchestration system\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## What Why\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nBorrowed from ultracode's quality patterns: adversarial verify \u2014 spawn N independent skeptics per finding, each prompted to REFUTE it, defaulting to refuted when uncertain, and kill the finding unless it survives a majority; and perspective-diverse verify \u2014 when a finding can fail in more than one way, give each verifier a distinct lens rather than N identical checks, because diversity catches failure modes redundancy cannot. DH's multi-perspective-review already has the diverse lenses (security, performance, quality, accessibility) but reviewers are framed as finders/approvers, not refuters, and there is no vote-threshold mechanic \u2014 a single reviewer's plausible-but-wrong finding, or approval, stands unchallenged.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nBorrowed from ultracode's quality patterns: adversarial verify \u2014 spawn N independent skeptics per finding, each prompted to REFUTE it, defaulting to refuted when uncertain, and kill the finding unless it survives a majority; and perspective-diverse verify \u2014 when a finding can fail in more than one way, give each verifier a distinct lens rather than N identical checks, because diversity catches failure modes redundancy cannot. DH's multi-perspective-review already has the diverse lenses (security, performance, quality, accessibility) but reviewers are framed as finders/approvers, not refuters, and there is no vote-threshold mechanic \u2014 a single reviewer's plausible-but-wrong finding, or approval, stands unchallenged.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Mitigates\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nPlausible-but-wrong review findings surviving into fix cycles (wasted work); single-reviewer blind spots on high-risk changes; confirmation bias in verification prompts.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefit Lands In\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nQuality-gate precision (fewer false findings actioned) and recall on high-risk changes.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nQuality-gate precision (fewer false findings actioned) and recall on high-risk changes.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Proposed Exploration\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\n1. Add a refute-framed verification pass for findings above a severity threshold: N verifiers each prompted to disprove the finding, kill unless it survives the vote.\\n2. Keep lens diversity \u2014 verifiers get distinct refutation angles (does it reproduce, is it exploitable, is it in scope), not N copies of the same prompt.\\n3. Gate the fan-out by risk so cost stays proportional (composes with #3103 \u2014 low-risk findings get one verifier, high-risk get the panel).\\n4. Trial on one plan's review cycle and compare actioned-finding precision against the current single-pass baseline.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\n1. Add a refute-framed verification pass for findings above a severity threshold: N verifiers each prompted to disprove the finding, kill unless it survives the vote.\\n2. Keep lens diversity \u2014 verifiers get distinct refutation angles (does it reproduce, is it exploitable, is it in scope), not N copies of the same prompt.\\n3. Gate the fan-out by risk so cost stays proportional (composes with #3103 \u2014 low-risk findings get one verifier, high-risk get the panel).\\n4. Trial on one plan's review cycle and compare actioned-finding precision against the current single-pass baseline.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n#3103 (hard composition \u2014 same risk gate sizes both review and verification); this repo's falsification-requirement rule (same epistemics, currently prose-only).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"7b838698610079afc452dde73ca8a93e9036351ec186f805b420c595bbbd1377\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQIqZLA\"}"}